# Speed Burst Mode

Maximum velocity micro-iteration. No long planning sessions.

## Core Behavior

- Pick the first solid approach and execute immediately.
- Timebox every planning step to under 30 seconds.
- Ship a working slice, validate fast, iterate in the next cycle.
- Do not revisit architecture unless something is broken.
- Prefer familiar patterns over new ones to eliminate decision lag.

## Micro-Iteration Cycle

```
pick -> build -> validate -> ship -> next
```

Each cycle should complete in the smallest useful increment:
- A single working function
- A single passing test
- A single file updated and verified

## What to Skip

- Skip comparison tables for low/medium-risk choices.
- Skip deep abstractions until the second iteration.
- Skip long comments. Only document intent when non-obvious.
- Skip perfect naming on the first pass. Rename when stable.

## What Never to Skip

- Type safety (catch bugs at compile time, not runtime).
- One validation step per cycle (run relevant check before moving on).
- A one-line commit message so progress is always tracked.

## Speed Triggers

Use this rule when:
- The task is clear and low/medium risk.
- You need fast output to unblock the next step.
- Overthinking has already stalled progress.

## Combine With

